[00:17.00]indignant a. 愤怒的，愤慨的 示例 ① Spain's indignados, or indignant ones, still going strong since their start in May, have a claim too. 西班牙的愤怒者们的示威游行自五月份开始以来仍然没有减弱， 他们也有自己的宣言。（The Economist） ② She was very indignant at what the man had said. 她对那个男人所说的话表示愤怒。
[00:24.80]survey n. 民意调查；勘测；全面评述 vt. 对…进行民意调查；审视； 勘测；鉴定 示例 ① The United States has almost all of the world's best universities. A recent Chinese survey ranks 35 American universities among the top 50, eight among the top 10. 美国拥有几乎所有世界上最好的大学。根据中国最近的一项调查，排名前50位的世界顶尖大学中，美国占了35 所，前10名里面美国大学占了8所。（2012. 6）② We surveyed 320 students and found that over three quarters would like to pursue further study. 我们对320名学生进行调查，发现有超过四分之三的学生表示希望继续深造。
[00:38.83]thrive v. 兴旺发达，繁荣，茁壮成长 示例 ① Organisations cannot thrive without being focused on their desired end results any more than an individual can thrive without goals to provide a sense of purpose. 企业如果不专注于所期望的最终结果就无法兴旺，就如同一个人如果找不到有意义的目标就无法进步一样。（2012. 6）② A business cannot thrive without good management. 没有良好的经营管理，公司就不会兴旺发达。
[00:46.41]initial a. 开始的，最初的‖n. 首字母 示例 ① Shenwu puts up the initial investment to install a heat exchanger that preheats the air going into the furnace, slashing the client's fuel costs. （北京）神雾公司会先期投资安装一个热转换器，对进入锅炉的空气预先加热，以此帮助客户降低燃料成本。（2007. 12）② You may encounter a lot of difficulties at the initial stage of learning a foreign language. 在学一门外语的开始阶段，你可能会碰上很多困难。
[00:54.69]drain v. 流光；耗尽‖n. 下水道；消耗，耗尽 示例 ① That's because quickly growing energy demand requires immense investment in new supply, not to mention the drain of rising energy prices. 这是因为快速增加的能源需求要求对新的供应进行巨大的投资，更不用说能源价格上升所耗费的财力了。（2007. 12）② He drained his parents of every cent. 他耗尽了父母的每一分钱。
[01:00.29]resemblance n. 相似，相像 示例 ① Until recently, the only known fossils of Precambrian animals were what is called the Ediacaran fauna—a handful of strange creatures found in Australia, Canada and the English Midlands that lived in the Ediacaran period, between 635m and 541m years ago, and which bear little resemblance to what came afterwards. 直到最近，唯一被人们发现的前寒武纪的动物化石叫做埃迪卡拉动物群—— 在澳大利亚、加拿大和英国内陆发现的生活在埃迪卡拉纪时期（6.35亿至5.41亿年前） 的少量奇怪生物，它们被证实与后来的生物没有一点相似之处。（The Economist）② He has a strong resemblance to his father. 他长得很像他的父亲。
[01:08.43]security n. 保护措施；保安部门；保证；安全； 抵押品；[pl.] 证券 示例 ① We do NOT believe that every time school-age children go outside, they need a security guard. 我们不相信学龄孩子每次外出时都需要一个保镖。（2009. 6） ② Job security has become a concern to most adults. 大多数成年人变得关心工作的稳定性。
[01:14.07]emotion n. 情感，情绪，激情 示例 ① Because parents are emotionally important to their children, they are typically a child's most powerful role models. 因为父母在情感方面对他们的孩子很重要，所以他们通常是对孩子最有影响力的榜样。（2013. 6）② He managed to control his emotions when he heard the news. 他听到这个消息的时候极力控制住了自己的情绪。
[01:20.51]intrinsic a. 固有的，内在的，本质的 示例 ① Rendering cash as pure information is the final denial of the notion that money has intrinsic value: what was once a carefully weighed piece of gold, silver or bronze has become simply a token. 将现金纯粹当作一种信息来支付最终否定了所谓货币具有内在价值的概念：货币曾是一块金条、银条或铜块，支付时需仔细称量，而现在它已变得只是一种象征而已。（The Economist）② The intrinsic value of a coin is usually more than the value of the metal it is made of. 一枚钱币的内在价值通常比铸造这枚钱币的金属的价值要大。
[01:30.54]scrap n. 碎片；小块；少量，一点儿 示例 ① Big business lobbies and trade unions used to scrap over immigration, with employers wanting cheaper labour, and unions fearing it. 大型商业游说团体和贸易联盟过去经常在移民问题上打得不可开交——雇主想要更廉价的劳动力，工会却害怕劳动力变得廉价。（The Economist）② They intended to scrap the plan of vacation. 他们打算放弃假期的计划。
[01:37.45]monthly a. 每月的；按月结算的‖ad. 每个月，每月一次‖n. 月刊 示例 ① EL POPOLA CHINIO, which means From People's China, is a monthly magazine in Esperanto and is read worldwide. EL POPOLA CHINIO，意思是 “来自人民中国”，是一份世界语月刊，读者遍布全球。（2010. 6）② Winters are cold here, with monthly averages below 20℃. 这里冬天很冷，月平均气温在零下20摄氏度以下。
[01:46.27]poetry n. 诗歌，诗集 示例 ① All I can do is gather up the shattered remains of my hope and love and in the debris of the world keep at least one small blaze of poetry burning. 我唯一能做的就是重拾起自己支离破碎的希望和爱，在世界的残垣断壁中呵护那一点诗意的火苗，至少让它能继续燃烧。（www.theatlantic.com）② She spent all her spare time reading poetry. 她所有的业余时间都用在阅读诗歌上。 语料 Painting is silent poetry, and poetry is a speaking picture. 画是无言之诗，诗是有声之画。（古希腊作家西蒙尼特斯）
[01:53.52]intelligent a. 聪明的；有才智的；有理解和学习能力的；智能的 示例 ① The power of self-honoring can help to break all the falsehoods you were programmed to believe—those that made you feel that you were not good enough, or strong enough, or intelligent enough to do what you truly desire. 以自我为荣的力量有助于打破所有你打算去相信的谎言——那些让你觉得自己不够好，不够强壮，或者不够聪明去做你真正渴望的事情的谎言。（2007. 6）② What you made is an intelligent decision. 你所做的是一个明智的决定。
[02:01.34]expand vt. 扩大，增加；扩展（业务） 示例 ① Expanding the three-year option may be difficult, but it may be less difficult than asking Congress for additional financial help, asking legislators for more state support, or asking students for even higher tuition payments. 扩大三年制的范围也许很难，但是比起向国会要求额外的资金援助、向立法者争取更多的国家支持或向学生收取更高的学费，它可能更容易一些。（2012. 6）② Could you expand upon the matter a little further? 你能再进一步谈谈这件事吗？
[02:06.70]mere a. 仅仅的，只不过；纯粹的 示例 ① These results should convince public officials that music classes are not a mere decoration, ripe for discarding in the budget crises that constantly trouble public schools. 这些结果应该能说服政府工作人员：音乐课不单纯是一个随时可能因为不断困扰公立学校的预算危机而被抛弃的摆设。（2012. 6）② The mere fact that he can come to class is encouraging. 他能来上课就已经不错了。
[02:12.47]guilty a. 感到内疚的，感到惭愧的；有罪责的 示例 ① In my opinion, anyone who takes another person's life intentionally is insane; however, that does not mean that the person isn't guilty of the crime or that he shouldn't pay society the debt he owes. 在我看来，任何故意伤害他人性命的人都是精神失常的；然而，这并不意味着这个人无须担当罪责或者不需要偿还他欠社会的债。（2008. 6）② I felt guilty about not getting a bachelor's degree. 没有拿到学士学位证书，我感到很内疚。
[02:19.15]senator n. 参议员 示例 ① In a plan presented in December with Ron Wyden, a Democratic senator, he proposed letting the elderly put their subsidy toward either a private plan or traditional Medicare. 在民主党参议员罗恩• 怀登12月提出的计划中，他建议老年人可以用政府津贴自行决定参保私人保险还是参保传统的医疗保险项目。（The Economist） ② He serves as a Democratic senator for Texas. 他是德克萨斯州的民主党参议员。
[02:26.95]derive v. 获得；追寻…的起源 示例 ① The strongest incentives for energy conservation will derive from the market itself. 对能源节约的最有效的刺激来自于市场本身。（2007. 12）② We derived knowledge from practice. 我们从实践中获得知识。
[02:31.45]confusion n. 困惑；混淆；困窘；混乱状态 示例 ① A trademark prevents others from using the identical or a similar word, name, or symbol to take advantage of the recognition and popularity of the brand or to create confusion in the marketplace. 商标能防止他人通过使用相同或相似的文字、 名称或符号来利用该品牌的认知度和知名度 （获利），或者给市场造成混乱。（2008. 12）② There is some confusion about what we should do next. 我们对下一步应该做什么有些困惑。
[02:39.97]graphic a. 图表的，绘画的；生动的‖n. 图表 示例 ① About a year ago, I flew to Singapore to join the writer Malcolm Gladwell, the fashion designer Marc Ecko and the graphic designer Stefan Sagmeister in addressing a group of advertising people on "Marketing to the Child of Tomorrow." 大约一年前，我飞抵新加坡，与作家马尔科姆•格拉德韦尔、时尚设计师马克•埃克以及平面设计师斯蒂芬•施德明一起给一群广告行业的人士讲授“向明天的孩子推销”的课程。（2012. 12）② The monitor kept a graphic record of school attendance. 班长用图表记录学生的出勤情况。
[02:47.11]simultaneous a. 同时发生（或进行）的，同步的 示例 ① Ebola Zaire seemed to erupt in over 50 villages simultaneously. 扎伊尔型埃博拉病毒似乎在50多个村庄同时爆发。（2013. 6）② She did an excellent job in simultaneous interpretation. 她同声传译做得很好。
[02:51.91]disaster n. 灾难，灾祸；不幸 示例 ① They'd lost their home and many or all of their possessions through fires, floods, earthquakes, or some other disaster. 他们在火灾、水灾、地震或某种其他灾难中失去了家园和许多抑或是所有的财产。（2006. 12）② The performance is totally a disaster. 这场演出演砸了。
[03:00.60]quest n. 探索，寻找，追求‖v. 探索，探求 示例 ① Job-hunting tasks gain added meaning as you sense their importance in your quest for a more meaningful work life. 如果你能够意识到求职的任务在寻找更有意义的工作和生活的过程中的重要性，那么它们就会具有额外的意义。（2007. 6）② Nothing will stop us in our quest for truth. 没有什么能够阻挡我们追求真理。
[03:06.86]array n. 大堆；陈列；一系列；衣服，服装 示例 ① People with autism are also said to have weak central coherence—the ability to synthesise an array of information, such as verbal and gestural cues in conversation. 自闭症患者据说也存在中心聚合能力较差的问题，即他们不能整合大量的信息，比如谈话中的话语或手势等信息。（New Scientist）② The era also gave birth to a whole array of new social problems. 那个时代还产生了一系列新的社会问题。
[03:13.58]committee n. 委员会 示例 A committee will be set up to look into the matter. 将要成立一个委员会对此事进行调查。
[03:19.63]compact v. 把…紧压在一起‖a. 袖珍的；紧凑的‖n. 协定 示例 ① Compact fluorescent lamps, or CFLs, not only use 75 to 80 percent less electricity than incandescent bulbs to generate the same amount of light, but they also last 10 times longer. 在发光效果相同的情况下，紧凑型荧光灯不但可以比白炽灯泡节约75%到80%的电力，而且其使用寿命也要长10倍。（2007. 12）② I have entered into a compact with my clients. 我与客户订立了一项契约。
[03:25.72]hemisphere n. （地球的）半球；（大脑的）半球；（球体的）半球 示例 ① Despite her own artistic bent, she lamented that human beings in the modern age were too much led by the "archaic", emotional right hemisphere of their brains. 虽然她（生物学家丽塔•李维• 蒙塔西妮）喜欢艺术，但她叹息现代人类太偏向他们“古老的”、情绪化的右脑。（The Economist）② The right hemisphere of our brain is the one that feels, perceives, tastes, and so forth. 我们大脑的右半球掌管感觉、认知、审美等。
[03:34.67]emphasis n. 强调；重读 示例 ① A study by Mannaz, a leadership development company, suggests that, while the bully-boy chief executive of old may not have been eradicated completely, there is a definite shift in emphasis towards less tough styles of management —at least in America and Europe. 领导力发展公司马南兹的一项研究显示，虽然过去那种粗暴的主管可能不会彻底消失，但是确实已有所改变，即强调采用不那么强硬的管理模式——至少在美国和欧洲是如此。（2011. 6）② Our English teacher places special emphasis on grammar. 我们英语老师特别强调语法。
[03:41.13]collide vi. 相撞；冲突 示例 ① 25 years ago, Ray Anderson, a single parent with a one-year-old son witnessed a terrible accident which took place when the driver of a truck ran a red light and collided with the car of Sandra Jenkens. 25年前，单身爸爸雷•安德森和他一岁大的儿子见证了一场可怕的事故——一辆卡车闯红灯与桑德拉•詹肯斯的轿车撞在了一起。（2007. 6）② If the aims of two countries collide, there may be a war. 如果两国的目标冲突，就可能发生战争。
[03:48.68]cassette n. 盒式磁带；胶卷盒 示例 ① Georgia's governor even proposed giving every newborn there a classical CD or cassette. 佐治亚州州长甚至提议给该州每一个新生儿发一张古典音乐CD或一盒古典音乐磁带。（2012. 6）② His two albums released on cassette have sold more than 20 million copies. 他的两张专辑的磁带销量突破了2000万。
[03:57.80]scratch v. 挠痒；抓破；刮坏；刮去；刮出刺耳声‖n. 划痕；搔痒 示例 ① They can attend to several things at once in the mental scratch pad called working memory, an essential skill in this era of multitasking. 他们可以在被叫做“工作存储器”的大脑暂存记忆区中同时兼顾几件事，在同时处理多项任务的时代，这是一种必不可少的技能。（2012. 6）② The athlete was scratched from the race because of a knee injury. 这个运动员由于膝盖受伤退出了比赛。
[04:05.65]shift v. 转移；推卸（责任）；换挡‖n. 转变；轮班；转换键 示例 ① Even so, the shift in the centre of gravity to older age groups is bound to have a profound effect on societies, not just economically and politically but in all sorts of other ways too. 即使这样，重心偏向老年群体肯定会对社会造成深远的影响， 这不仅是经济和政治上的，对其他各个方面都会有影响。（2010. 12）② He shifted the blame for his mistakes onto his classmates. 他把自己犯的错转嫁到了同学身上。
[04:13.15]counter v. 反驳；抵制‖n. 柜台；反驳‖ad. 逆向地，相反地 示例 ① Schweitzer concedes his research runs counter to a very large body of literature that commends the many benefits of goal-setting. 施魏策尔承认他的研究与大量推崇目标设定有诸多好处的文献正好相反。（2012. 6）② Those drugs are sold under the counter. 那些药品是私下贩卖的。
[04:17.43]mysterious a. 神秘的；故弄玄虚的 示例 ① As recently as 40,000 years ago there were three other species of human on Earth: Neanderthals in Europe, the "hobbits" of Flores, in Indonesia, and a recently discovered and still mysterious group of creatures called the Denisovans, who lived in Central Asia. 早在4万年前，地球上还存在另外三个人种：欧洲的尼安德塔人，印度尼西亚佛洛里斯岛上的“霍比特人”，以及最近才发现的一个叫丹尼索瓦人的神秘人种，该人种曾居住在中亚。（The Economist）② There are many mysterious stories about the Egyptian pyramids. 关于埃及金字塔有许多神秘的故事。
[04:25.49]publicity n. 为公众所知、所见之状况；宣传（业务）；传播工作 示例 ① Many small, family-owned shipping firms have publicity-shy bosses and lack the sophisticated public-relations machines that giant firms deploy. 许多小型家族航运公司的老板不愿意曝光， 这使得他们缺少大型公司所拥有的复杂的公共关系网络。（The Economist）② He released an article under a fictitious name to avoid publicity. 他用虚构的名字发表文章以避免引起公众注意。
[04:33.60]foster vt. 促进；抚育‖a. 通过收养而产生家庭关系的 示例 ① Those who perform best on the sports field can take the Sporting PLuS Award which fosters employer-friendly sports accomplishments. 那些在运动领域表现最佳的学生能获得Sporting PLuS奖，这一奖项旨在培养雇主看重的体育技能。（2011. 6）② Your foster mother is a warm person. 你养母是个热心的人。
[04:39.21]bond n. 关系；债券；连接‖v. 使牢固结合； 建立互信关系 示例 ① A fresh indicator of market confidence in European borrowers will come as Italy sells billions of euros in bonds this week. 本周意大利发放数十亿欧元债券，这将是市场对欧洲债主的信任的一个新的暗示。（The New York Times）② Common tastes form a bond between the two men. 共同的爱好使两人结交。 语料 No man can sever the bonds that unite him to his society simply by averting his eyes. 没有人仅凭闭目、不看社会现实就能割断自己与社会的联系。（美国前总统富兰克林•罗斯福）
[04:47.03]plentiful a. 大量的，充裕的，丰富的 示例 ① Bodies that expected food to be plentiful, by contrast, should ration themselves to avoid the consequences of chronic overeating. 与此相反，对于想吃大量食物的人，则应该约束自己以避开长期性饮食过量。（The Economist）② Pineapple are plentiful in this season. 这个季节盛产菠萝。
[04:52.53]theoretical a. 理论上的；理论上存在的，假设的 示例 ① You are encouraged to develop your own individual responses to various practical and theoretical issues, which are raised by studying how speakers and writers employ English for a wide variety of purposes. 鼓励你们通过研究演说家和作家如何用英语来表达各种各样的目的，来培养你对各种不同的实用性和理论性问题的个人应变能力。（2009. 6）② This kind of application is still theoretical. 这种应用目前只停留在理论层面。
[05:00.38]utmost a. 最大的，极度的‖n. 最大限度，极限，最大可能 示例 ① British politicians, led by the Conservatives, do their utmost to signal hostility and mislead the public. 以保守党为代表的英国政客正竭尽全力显示敌意并误导社会公众。
